In this test, we are using the shallow rendering method of Enzyme to render the <App /> component and then checking if it contains the <Form /> and <ContactDetails /> components using the `find()` method. We then use the `toHaveLength()` method to confirm the number of instances of each component. This test will pass if both components are found and will fail if either of them is missing.

Here are example Jest tests for the <Form /> and <ContactDetails /> components:

```js
import React from 'react';
import { shallow } from 'enzyme';
import Form from './Form';
import ContactDetails from './ContactDetails';

describe('<Form />', () => {
  it('renders a form with input fields', () => {
    const wrapper = shallow(<Form />);
    expect(wrapper.find('form')).toHaveLength(1);
    expect(wrapper.find('input')).toHaveLength(2);
  });

  it('updates state when input values change', () => {
