    const wrapper = shallow(<ContactDetails firstName="John" lastName="Doe" />);
    expect(wrapper.containsMatchingElement(<h2>John Doe</h2>)).toEqual(true);
  });

  it('displays a message if no name is provided', () => {
    const wrapper = shallow(<ContactDetails />);
    expect(wrapper.containsMatchingElement(<h2>Please provide a name.</h2>)).toEqual(true);
  });
});
```

In the first test for <Form />, we are checking if the component renders a <form> element with two <input> fields. In the second test, we are simulating a change event on both input fields and checking if the component's state is updated correctly.

For <ContactDetails />, we have two tests. The first checks if the component displays the user's name correctly based on the props passed in. The second test checks if the component displays a message asking for a name if no name is provided via props. 

Note that these are just example tests and you may need to modify them based on the specific implementation of your <Form /> and <ContactDetails /> components.

