    ]
  ),
)
```

The `Expanded` widget causes its child to expand to fill the available space inside its parent. By wrapping the `Row` widget inside an `Expanded`, the `Row` will expand horizontally to fill the width of its parent container.

You can adjust the `flex` property of the `Expanded` widget to change the ratio of how much space each child widget should occupy within the `Row`. For example, setting `flex: 1` on two child widgets inside a `Row` will cause them to occupy equal space.

```dart
Row(
