The `printf` function in C language is used to print the output to the console. It can print different types of data like integers, floats, characters, and strings. However, it does not have an option to directly print in binary format. 

To print an integer in binary format, we need to convert it to binary first and then print it. The following code snippet can be used to print an integer in binary format using `printf`: 

```c
void printBinary(int num){
    int binaryNum[32];
    int i = 0;
    while(num > 0){
        binaryNum[i] = num % 2;
        num = num / 2;
        i++;
    }
    for(int j=i-1; j>=0; j--){
        printf("%d", binaryNum[j]);
    }
}
```

This function takes an integer as input and converts it to binary format using the modulo-2 division method. It then prints the binary digits in reverse order. 

To print binary format for other types of data, we can first convert them to integer format and then use the above function to print them in binary.

