Here's a revised version of the `diag()` function to create a diagonal matrix of a specified size with a given 1D array as the diagonal:

```c
double** diag(int rows, double* array) {
    double** matrix = (double**)malloc(rows * sizeof(double*));
    int i, j;
    for (i = 0; i < rows; ++i) {
        matrix[i] = (double*)malloc(rows * sizeof(double));
        for (j = 0; j < rows; ++j) {
            if (i == j) {
                matrix[i][j] = array[i % rows];
            } else {
                matrix[i][j] = 0.0;
            }
        }
    }
    return matrix;
}
```

In this revised implementation, the size of the diagonal is determined by the length of the input `array`, and it is repeated cyclically along the diagonal of the target `rows * rows` matrix using the modulo operator `%`.

