If an item has children tags, the XmlPullParser will automatically read them as it goes through the XML file. When it encounters a start tag, it will trigger the `START_TAG` event and read its attributes and child tags. When it encounters an end tag, it will trigger the `END_TAG` event and move on to the next tag.

For example, if your XML file looks like this:

```
