    <name>Item 1</name>
    <description>A description of item 1</description>
  </item>
  <item id="102">
    <name>Item 2</name>
    <description>A description of item 2</description>
  </item>
</items>
```

The `readItemsFromXml` function I provided in my previous answer would also read the `name` and `description` tags as it goes through the XML file. The `itemId` variable will be set to the `id` property of the current "item" tag, and you can use additional variables to keep track of the current item's name and description.

Here's an updated version of the function that demonstrates this:

```
private fun readItemsFromXml(xmlString: String) {
    val factory = XmlPullParserFactory.newInstance()
    val parser = factory.newPullParser()
    parser.setInput(StringReader(xmlString))

    var eventType = parser.eventType
    var itemId: String? = null
    var itemName: String? = null
    var itemDescription: String? = null

    while (eventType != XmlPullParser.END_DOCUMENT) {
        when (eventType) {
            XmlPullParser.START_TAG -> {
                when (parser.name) {
                    "item" -> {
                        // This is an "item" tag, so read its "id" property
                        itemId = parser.getAttributeValue(null, "id")
                    }
                    "name" -> {
                        // This is a "name" tag, so read its text content
                        itemName = parser.nextText()
                    }
                    "description" -> {
                        // This is a "description" tag, so read its text content
                        itemDescription = parser.nextText()
                    }
                }
            }
            XmlPullParser.END_TAG -> {
                if (parser.name == "item") {
                    // We have finished reading one "item" tag, so do something with its properties
                    handleItem(itemId, itemName, itemDescription)
                    itemId = null
                    itemName = null
                    itemDescription = null
                }
            }
        }
        eventType = parser.next()
    }
}

private fun handleItem(itemId: String?, itemName: String?, itemDescription: String?) {
    // Do something with the item properties (e.g. print them to the console)
    if (itemId != null && itemName != null && itemDescription != null) {
        Log.d(TAG, "Found item with id=$itemId, name=$itemName, description=$itemDescription")
    }
}
```

