    private List<BlogPost> posts;

    // getters and setters
}
```

In the above example, the BlogPost is the source entity and the User is the target entity. The `@ManyToOne` annotation on the BlogPost entity indicates that many BlogPosts can be associated with a single User, and the `@JoinColumn` annotation specifies the Foreign Key column to link the two entities. The `mappedBy` attribute on the User entity tells JPA to use the "user" field on the BlogPost entity as the mappedBy attribute to link the two entities.

2. @OneToMany:

Consider the following example of a customer and their orders. A customer can have many orders, but an order can only belong to one customer.

```java
@Entity
