The error indicates that the anisotropic sampling feature is not enabled for your chosen physical device. In order to fix this issue, you should first check if the GPU supports anisotropic sampling and then enable it in the VkPhysicalDeviceFeatures struct before creating the logical device.

Here are the steps to perform this:

1. After choosing the physical device and before creating the device, query the physical device features to check if samplerAnisotropy is supported:

```cpp
VkPhysicalDeviceFeatures supportedFeatures;
vkGetPhysicalDeviceFeatures(physicalDevice, &supportedFeatures);

if (!supportedFeatures.samplerAnisotropy) {
    throw std::runtime_error("Selected GPU does not support anisotropic filtering");
}
```

2. Enable samplerAnisotropy in the VkPhysicalDeviceFeatures struct `deviceFeatures` before creating the logical device:

```cpp
// Set up the physical device features
VkPhysicalDeviceFeatures deviceFeatures{};
deviceFeatures.samplerAnisotropy = VK_TRUE; // Enable anisotropic filtering
```

