To avoid the type errors, we use `compareBy` to create a comparator that extracts and compares the second or third child view (i.e., the `TextView` containing the name or year value) of each `TableRow` object.

We then pass the comparator to the `sortedWith()` function of the `List` object to perform the sorting. The `reversed()` function is called on the comparator for descending order sorting.

