}
```

This code declares two vectors `vec1` and `vec2`, which we want to join. We use the `std::views::concat` function to concatenate them efficiently. The `merged` variable is now a view object representing a concatenated range of `vec1` and `vec2`.

Then we loop through the `merged` view and print out the combined elements for each vector, separated by a space.

Using `std::views::concat` provides a way to join two vectors without creating a new vector in memory. The `merged` view only provides a concatenation of the two input vectors.

