To call an array from another class in Java, you first need to declare the array as a public field or create a public getter method for the array in the class where it is defined. 

For example,

```java
public class ArrayClass {
    public int[] array = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};
}

```

Then, in the class where you want to access the array, you create an instance of the ArrayClass and use dot notation to access the array field or use the getter method.

For example,

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        ArrayClass arrayClass = new ArrayClass();
        int[] myArray = arrayClass.array;
        // Alternatively, you can use a getter method
        // int[] myArray = arrayClass.getArray();
        // Use myArray
    }
}
```

In this example, we create an instance of ArrayClass called arrayClass and access its public array field using dot notation to store it in a new array called myArray. Alternatively, you can create a public getter method in ArrayClass that returns the array to be accessed from the main class.

