To execute a .NET application from PHP and call the DLL, you can use the `shell_exec()` function to run the .NET application and pass the path to the DLL. Here's a step-by-step guide on how to do this:

1. Create a .NET application (e.g., console application in C#) that loads and calls the specific DLL function you want to use. Here's a simple example:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Reflection;

namespace DotNetAppToCallDLL
{
    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            if (args.Length < 1)
            {
                Console.WriteLine("Provide path to DLL as an argument.");
                return;
            }

            string dllPath = args[0];

            Assembly assembly = Assembly.LoadFrom(dllPath);
            Type type = assembly.GetType("NamespaceName.ClassName"); // Replace with the DLL's namespace and class name
            MethodInfo method = type.GetMethod("MethodName"); // Replace with the DLL's method name

            object instance = Activator.CreateInstance(type);
            object result = method.Invoke(instance, new object[] { /* method arguments */ });

            Console.WriteLine("Result: " + result.ToString());
        }
    }
}
```

2. Compile the .NET application and generate an executable file (e.g., `DotNetAppToCallDLL.exe`).

3. In your PHP script, use the `shell_exec()` function to call the .NET application and pass the path to the DLL that you want to load:

```php
<?php
$exePath = "path/to/DotNetAppToCallDLL.exe";
$dllPath = "path/to/yourDLL.dll";

$output = shell_exec("$exePath $dllPath");
echo $output;
?>
```

4. Finally, run your PHP script to execute the .NET application and call the DLL function.

To create a PHP website that allows users to upload video files, convert them to MP4, and start the download automatically, you'll need to follow these steps:

1. Install and set up a PHP server (e.g., Apache, NGINX) if you haven't already.

2. Install FFmpeg (https://www.ffmpeg.org/) on your server to handle video conversion to MP4.

3. Create an HTML form to let users upload their video files.

4. Handle file uploads and video conversion in PHP.

5. Use JavaScript to trigger download links automatically upon completion of file conversion.

Here's an example of how you might structure the code for each of these steps:

1. HTML form for uploading the video:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Video Uploader</title>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Upload your video file</h1>
  <form action="upload.php" method="POST" enctype="multipart/form-data">
    <input type="file" name="video" accept="video/*"/><br>
    <button type="submit" name="submit">Upload</button>
  </form>
</body>
</html>
```

2. PHP script to handle file uploads and video conversion (upload.php):

```php
<?php
  if (isset($_POST['submit'])) {
    $uploadDirectory = 'uploads/';

    $filename = $_FILES['video']['name'];
    $tmpName = $_FILES['video']['tmp_name'];
    $error = $_FILES['video']['error'];

    if ($error === UPLOAD_ERR_OK) {
      $destination = $uploadDirectory . $filename;

      if (move_uploaded_file($tmpName, $destination)) {

        $outputFile = $uploadDirectory . uniqid('converted_') . '.mp4';

        $command = 'ffmpeg -i ' . escapeshellarg($destination) . ' -c:v libx264 -crf 23 -c:a aac -strict -2 -b:a 192k -aspect 16:9 ' . escapeshellarg($outputFile) . ' 2>&1';
        exec($command, $output, $status);

        if ($status === 0) {
          unlink($destination);

          // Return the download link
          header('Content-Type: application/json');
          echo json_encode(['result' => 'success', 'file' => $outputFile]);

        } else {
          echo 'Failed to convert the video. FFmpeg output: ' . implode("\n", $output);
        }

      } else {
        echo 'File move failed';
      }

    } else {
      echo 'Upload error';
    }
  }
?>
```

3. JavaScript to trigger the download automatically (add this in the HTML file inside the `head`):

```html
<head>
  ...
  <script>
    document.querySelector('form').addEventListener('submit', function(event) {
      event.preventDefault();

      var formData = new FormData(this);
      fetch('upload.php', {
        method: 'POST',
        body: formData
      })
        .then(response => response.json())
        .then(data => {
          if (data.result === 'success') {
            var a = document.createElement('a');
            a.href = data.file;
            a.download = '';
            document.body.appendChild(a);
            a.click();
            document.body.removeChild(a);
          } else {
            alert('Error converting the video');
          }
        });
    });
  </script>
</head>
```

This example script creates an HTML form to upload video files and processes the video file with FFmpeg after uploading. Once the conversion is complete, a download link will be returned by the PHP script, and JavaScript will automatically trigger the download. Ensure that you have write permissions in the 'uploads' directory on your server.

You can use the `unwrap_or()` method to get the value if it exists or to use the default value otherwise. Here is an example:

```rust
let my_string: Option<String> = Some("hello".to_string());

// Get the value if it exists or default to an empty string
let result = my_string.unwrap_or("".to_string());

println!("{}", result); // prints "hello"

let other_string: Option<String> = None;

// Get the value if it exists or default to an empty string
let result = other_string.unwrap_or("".to_string());

println!("{}", result); // prints ""
```

In this example, we use `unwrap_or()` to get the value of `my_string` or default to an empty string (`""`). The result is `"hello"`. We also use `unwrap_or()` with `other_string` to get the default value since it is `None`. The result is an empty string (`""`).

import {useCallback, useEffect, useState} from "react";
import {ReadyState} from "../enums/readyState";

type CupItem = {
  futures_price_micro: number;
  quantity: number;
  spot_quantity: number;
  side: string;
};

export interface BestMicroPrice {
  buy: number;
  sell: number;
}

export function useRustWsServer() {
  const [connection, setConnection] = useState<WebSocket|null>(null);
  const [readyState, setReadyState] = useState(0);
  const [cup, setCup] = useState<Array<CupItem>>([]);
  const [bestMicroPrice, setBestMicroPrice] = useState<BestMicroPrice|null>(null);
  const [maxVolume, setMaxVolume] = useState(1);

  function splitCupSides(rawData: {[key: number]: CupItem}): Array<CupItem> {
    const sellRecords = [];
    const buyRecords = [];
    let max = 0;

    for (const value of Object.values(rawData)) {
      if (value.side === "Buy") {
        buyRecords.push(value);
      } else if (value.side === "Sell") {
        sellRecords.push(value);
      }

      if (value.quantity > max) {
        max = value.quantity;
      }
    }

    sellRecords.sort((a, b) => {
      return b.futures_price_micro - a.futures_price_micro;
    });

    buyRecords.sort((a, b) => {
      return b.futures_price_micro - a.futures_price_micro;
    });

    setMaxVolume(max);

    return [...sellRecords, ...buyRecords];
  }

  const cupSubscribe = useCallback((symbol: string, camera: number, zoom: number, rowCount: number) => {
    if (null === connection || readyState !== ReadyState.OPEN) return;

    connection.send(JSON.stringify({
      "commands": [
        {
          commandType: "SUBSCRIBE_SYMBOL",
          symbol,
          camera: Math.round(camera / zoom) * zoom,
          zoom,
          rowCount,
        },
      ],
    }));
  }, [readyState]);

  const cupUnsubscribe = useCallback((symbol: string) => {
    if (null === connection || readyState !== ReadyState.OPEN) return;

    connection.send(JSON.stringify({
      "commands": [
        {
          commandType: "UNSUBSCRIBE_SYMBOL",
          symbol,
        },
      ],
    }));
  }, [readyState]);

  useEffect(() => {
    const url = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_RUST_WS_SERVER;

    if (url) {
      const ws = new WebSocket(url);

      setConnection(ws);
    }
  }, []);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (null !== connection) {

      connection.onmessage = (message: MessageEvent) => {
        if (!message.data) return;

        const data = JSON.parse(message.data);

        if (!data?.commands || data.commands.length === 0) return;

        const domUpdate = data.commands.find((item: any) => "undefined" !== typeof item.SymbolDomUpdate);

        if (!domUpdate) return;

        setCup(splitCupSides(domUpdate.SymbolDomUpdate.dom_rows));
        setBestMicroPrice({
          buy: domUpdate.SymbolDomUpdate.best_prices_futures.best_ask_micro,
          sell: domUpdate.SymbolDomUpdate.best_prices_futures.best_bid_micro,
        });
      };

      connection.onopen = () => {
        setReadyState(ReadyState.OPEN);
      };

      connection.onclose = () => {
        setReadyState(ReadyState.CLOSED);
      };
    }
  }, [connection]);

  return {
    readyState,
    cupSubscribe,
    cupUnsubscribe,
    cup,
    maxVolume,
    bestMicroPrice,
  };
}

