1. Change the reward system: Instead of giving a negative reward when the agent is near a wall, you can simply not move the agent and not give any reward in that case. This way, the agent will not have a strong negative incentive to avoid the walls.

2. Add distance to the nearest wall to the agent's observations: The agent may become better at navigating near walls if it has more information about its surroundings.

