The issue might be caused by trying to allocate descriptor sets with an exhausted descriptor pool or an incorrect descriptor pool configuration. Since you are creating descriptor sets inside the Render() function, you need to make sure you're not exceeding the maximum set limit specified in your descriptor pool.

I can see that you're creating the descriptor pool with maxSets set to 1:

```cpp
VkDescriptorPool descriptorPool = renderer.CreateDescriptorPool(1);
```

I recommend increasing the maxSets value to account for multiple descriptors per frame, e.g., kMaxFramesInFlight * N, where N is the number of descriptor sets you expect per frame. You should also adjust the descriptor pool size accordingly in the CreateDescriptorPool function.

