2. Calculate the minimum and maximum x and y coordinates of the vertices.

```cpp
float minX = worldVertices[0], minY = worldVertices[1];
float maxX = worldVertices[0], maxY = worldVertices[1];

for (int i = 2; i < verticesCount * 8; i += 2) {
    float x = worldVertices[i];
    float y = worldVertices[i + 1];

    if (x < minX) minX = x;
    if (y < minY) minY = y;
    if (x > maxX) maxX = x;
    if (y > maxY) maxY = y;
}
```

3. Calculate the center point by averaging the minimum and maximum values.

```cpp
float centerX = (minX + maxX) / 2;
float centerY = (minY + maxY) / 2;
```

